IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-bodies`
IMPORT `uc3-disability-payments`
IMPORT `uc3-sch1-interpretation`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-interpretation`
IMPORT `uc3-sch3-occupation`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedule 3 (claimant treated as occupying or not occupying accommodation): tests of layer 1.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text).
--
-- EVERY EXPECTED VALUE IS WRITTEN HERE FROM THE TEXT, beside the assertion, before the file was run: none was copied from what the encoding printed.
-- The month limits (one month in paragraphs 5, 7 and 8; 12 months in 6; 6 and 12 months in 9) follow the counting convention of fork U3-F8 in NOTES.md:
-- a period that starts on 1 January 2025 has lasted one month on 31 January and exceeds it on 1 February; six months on 30 June and exceeds them on 1 July;
-- 12 months on 31 December 2025 and exceeds them on 1 January 2026.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Helpers.

GIVEN received IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Disability payments of a person`
`uc3 test — a person who may receive the daily living component of personal independence payment` received MEANS
    `Disability payments of a person` WITH
        `care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate` IS `neither received nor so entitled`
        `care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations` IS `neither received nor so entitled`
        `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` IS `neither received nor so entitled`
        `attendance allowance` IS `neither received nor so entitled`
        `pension age disability payment` IS `neither received nor so entitled`
        `daily living component of personal independence payment` IS IF received THEN `received by the person` ELSE `neither received nor so entitled`
        `daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate` IS `neither received nor so entitled`

GIVEN isClaimantOrChild IS A BOOLEAN
      received IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person who may be specified in paragraph 5(3)`
`uc3 test — a person who may be specified` isClaimantOrChild received MEANS
    `Person who may be specified in paragraph 5(3)` WITH
        `a claimant or any child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible` IS isClaimantOrChild
        payments IS `uc3 test — a person who may receive the daily living component of personal independence payment` received

GIVEN isCareHome IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Premises that may be a care home`
`uc3 test — premises that may be a care home` isCareHome MEANS
    `Premises that may be a care home` WITH
        `nation of Great Britain in which the premises are` IS England
        `a care home within the meaning of section 3 of the Care Standards Act 2000` IS isCareHome
        `a place at which a care home service within the meaning of Part 1 of the Regulation and Inspection of Social Care (Wales) Act 2016 is provided wholly or mainly to persons aged 18 or over` IS FALSE
        `a care home service within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 12 to the Public Services Reform (Scotland) Act 2010` IS FALSE
        `the premises as a hospital that may be an independent hospital` IS `Hospital that may be an independent hospital` WITH
            `a hospital as defined by section 275 of the National Health Service Act 2006` IS FALSE
            `a health service hospital as defined by section 275 of the National Health Service Act 2006` IS FALSE
            `an independent hospital as the meaning is assigned to it by section 2 of the Care Standards Act 2000` IS FALSE
            `an independent health care service as defined in section 10F(1)(a) and (b) of the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978` IS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 1: the general rule. A claimant is treated as occupying as their home the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home, and no accommodation of more than one dwelling.
-- Expected: the accommodation normally occupied and of one dwelling gives TRUE; of two dwellings gives FALSE; not the accommodation normally occupied gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 1 — the claimant is treated as occupying the accommodation as their home` (`Accommodation the claimant may occupy as their home` WITH `the accommodation is the accommodation which the claimant normally occupies as their home` IS TRUE, `number of dwellings the accommodation comprises` IS 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 1 — the claimant is treated as occupying the accommodation as their home` (`Accommodation the claimant may occupy as their home` WITH `the accommodation is the accommodation which the claimant normally occupies as their home` IS TRUE, `number of dwellings the accommodation comprises` IS 2) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 1 — the claimant is treated as occupying the accommodation as their home` (`Accommodation the claimant may occupy as their home` WITH `the accommodation is the accommodation which the claimant normally occupies as their home` IS FALSE, `number of dwellings the accommodation comprises` IS 1) EQUALS FALSE

-- Paragraph 2: croft land used for the purposes of accommodation normally occupied as a home, situated on or pertaining to a croft, is treated as included. Expected: all three TRUE; each missing FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 2 — the croft land is treated as included in the accommodation` (`Accommodation that may be on a croft` WITH `the accommodation is the accommodation which the claimant normally occupies as their home` IS TRUE, `the accommodation is situated on or pertains to a croft within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Crofters (Scotland) Act 1993` IS TRUE, `the croft land is used for the purposes of the accommodation` IS TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 2 — the croft land is treated as included in the accommodation` (`Accommodation that may be on a croft` WITH `the accommodation is the accommodation which the claimant normally occupies as their home` IS FALSE, `the accommodation is situated on or pertains to a croft within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Crofters (Scotland) Act 1993` IS TRUE, `the croft land is used for the purposes of the accommodation` IS TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 2 — the croft land is treated as included in the accommodation` (`Accommodation that may be on a croft` WITH `the accommodation is the accommodation which the claimant normally occupies as their home` IS TRUE, `the accommodation is situated on or pertains to a croft within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Crofters (Scotland) Act 1993` IS FALSE, `the croft land is used for the purposes of the accommodation` IS TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 2 — the croft land is treated as included in the accommodation` (`Accommodation that may be on a croft` WITH `the accommodation is the accommodation which the claimant normally occupies as their home` IS TRUE, `the accommodation is situated on or pertains to a croft within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Crofters (Scotland) Act 1993` IS TRUE, `the croft land is used for the purposes of the accommodation` IS FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

-- Paragraph 3: a claimant required to move out for essential repairs who intends to return, meeting the payment and liability conditions for either the other accommodation or the home (but not both),
-- is treated as normally occupying the one for which they are met; if both are met, the general rule applies (3(2)).
GIVEN required IS A BOOLEAN
      returns IS A BOOLEAN
      other IS A BOOLEAN
      home IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Claimant living in other accommodation during essential repairs`
`uc3 test — a claimant during essential repairs` required returns other home MEANS
    `Claimant living in other accommodation during essential repairs` WITH
        `the claimant is required to move into the other accommodation on account of essential repairs being carried out to the accommodation the claimant normally occupies as their home` IS required
        `the claimant intends to return to the accommodation which is under repair` IS returns
        `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the other accommodation` IS other
        `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home` IS home
-- Expected: only the other accommodation gives the other accommodation; only the accommodation under repair gives that one; both gives the general rule; neither gives the general rule;
-- not required to move out gives the general rule; not intending to return gives the general rule.
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 3 — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying` (`uc3 test — a claimant during essential repairs` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `the other accommodation`
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 3 — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying` (`uc3 test — a claimant during essential repairs` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `the accommodation under repair`
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 3 — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying` (`uc3 test — a claimant during essential repairs` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `the general rule in paragraph 1 applies`
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 3 — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying` (`uc3 test — a claimant during essential repairs` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the general rule in paragraph 1 applies`
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 3 — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying` (`uc3 test — a claimant during essential repairs` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `the general rule in paragraph 1 applies`
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 3 — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying` (`uc3 test — a claimant during essential repairs` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `the general rule in paragraph 1 applies`

-- Paragraph 4: housed in two dwellings by a provider of social housing on account of the number of children and qualifying young persons; normally occupies both with them;
-- meets the payment and liability conditions for both. Expected: all five gives TRUE; each missing gives FALSE; a landlord that is not a provider of social housing gives FALSE.
GIVEN provider IS A BOOLEAN
      housed IS A BOOLEAN
      both IS A BOOLEAN
      conditionsA IS A BOOLEAN
      conditionsB IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Claimant housed in two dwellings by a provider of social housing`
`uc3 test — a claimant housed in two dwellings` provider housed both conditionsA conditionsB MEANS
    `Claimant housed in two dwellings by a provider of social housing` WITH
        `the provider of social housing that housed the claimant` IS `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing` WITH
            `the landlord as a possible local authority` IS `Body that may be a local authority` WITH
                `nation of Great Britain in relation to which it is asked` IS England
                `kind of body` IS `another kind of body`
            `non-profit registered provider of social housing` IS provider
            `profit-making registered provider of social housing` IS FALSE
            `the accommodation is social housing` IS FALSE
            `the landlord as a possible registered social landlord` IS `Landlord that may be a registered social landlord` WITH
                `registered in the register maintained by the Welsh Ministers under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Housing Act 1996` IS FALSE
                `registered in the register maintained by the Scottish Housing Regulator under section 20(1) of the Housing (Scotland) Act 2010` IS FALSE
        `the claimant has been housed in two dwellings on account of the number of children and qualifying young persons living with the claimant` IS housed
        `the claimant normally occupies both accommodation A and accommodation B with children or qualifying young persons for whom the claimant is responsible` IS both
        `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of accommodation A` IS conditionsA
        `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of accommodation B` IS conditionsB
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 4 — both dwellings are treated as the single accommodation the claimant normally occupies as their home` (`uc3 test — a claimant housed in two dwellings` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 4 — both dwellings are treated as the single accommodation the claimant normally occupies as their home` (`uc3 test — a claimant housed in two dwellings` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 4 — both dwellings are treated as the single accommodation the claimant normally occupies as their home` (`uc3 test — a claimant housed in two dwellings` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 4 — both dwellings are treated as the single accommodation the claimant normally occupies as their home` (`uc3 test — a claimant housed in two dwellings` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 4 — both dwellings are treated as the single accommodation the claimant normally occupies as their home` (`uc3 test — a claimant housed in two dwellings` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 4 — both dwellings are treated as the single accommodation the claimant normally occupies as their home` (`uc3 test — a claimant housed in two dwellings` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

-- Paragraph 5(3): a person specified is a claimant, or a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible, in receipt of one of the seven payments.
-- Expected: a claimant or child receiving one of them gives TRUE; one not receiving gives FALSE; a person who is neither claimant nor child gives FALSE even if receiving.
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5(3) — a person is specified` (`uc3 test — a person who may be specified` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5(3) — a person is specified` (`uc3 test — a person who may be specified` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5(3) — a person is specified` (`uc3 test — a person who may be specified` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE

-- Paragraph 5: moving home, adaptations for a disabled person. miss: 0 nothing missing; 1 not yet moved in; 2 conditions not met before the move; 3 no necessary delay; 4 the person is not specified;
-- 5 not entitled to the housing costs element for the old accommodation before the move; 6 the delay was not reasonable. first: the first day treated as occupying both; day: the day asked about.
GIVEN miss IS A NUMBER
      first IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Move to a new home that is adapted for a disabled person`
`uc3 test — a move to an adapted home` miss first day MEANS
    `Move to a new home that is adapted for a disabled person` WITH
        `the claimant has moved into the new accommodation` IS NOT (miss EQUALS 1)
        `immediately before the move, the claimant met the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the new accommodation` IS NOT (miss EQUALS 2)
        `there was a delay in moving in that was necessary to enable the new accommodation to be adapted to meet the disablement needs of a specified person` IS NOT (miss EQUALS 3)
        `the specified person` IS `uc3 test — a person who may be specified` TRUE (NOT (miss EQUALS 4))
        `immediately before the move, the claimant was entitled to the inclusion of the housing costs element in an award of universal credit in respect of the old accommodation` IS NOT (miss EQUALS 5)
        `the delay in moving into the new accommodation was reasonable` IS NOT (miss EQUALS 6)
        `first day on which the claimant is treated as occupying both accommodations` IS first
        `day to which the question relates` IS day
-- Expected: nothing missing, on the first day or within the month (31 January 2025 for a first day of 1 January 2025) gives TRUE; on 1 February 2025 (more than one month, 5(4)) gives FALSE;
-- each of the six missing in turn gives FALSE (1, 2, 3, 4 through 5(1); 5 and 6 through 5(2)).
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5 — the claimant is treated as occupying both the new and the old accommodation` (`uc3 test — a move to an adapted home` 0 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5 — the claimant is treated as occupying both the new and the old accommodation` (`uc3 test — a move to an adapted home` 0 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 31)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5 — the claimant is treated as occupying both the new and the old accommodation` (`uc3 test — a move to an adapted home` 0 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 2 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5 — the claimant is treated as occupying both the new and the old accommodation` (`uc3 test — a move to an adapted home` 1 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5 — the claimant is treated as occupying both the new and the old accommodation` (`uc3 test — a move to an adapted home` 2 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5 — the claimant is treated as occupying both the new and the old accommodation` (`uc3 test — a move to an adapted home` 3 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5 — the claimant is treated as occupying both the new and the old accommodation` (`uc3 test — a move to an adapted home` 4 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5 — the claimant is treated as occupying both the new and the old accommodation` (`uc3 test — a move to an adapted home` 5 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5 — the claimant is treated as occupying both the new and the old accommodation` (`uc3 test — a move to an adapted home` 6 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5(1) — sub-paragraph (2) applies` (`uc3 test — a move to an adapted home` 5 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 5(2) — conditions for being treated as occupying both` (`uc3 test — a move to an adapted home` 6 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 6: living in other accommodation because of a reasonable fear of violence.
-- apply: 0 the paragraph applies; 1 the claimant is not occupying other accommodation; 2 it is not unreasonable to expect a return; 3 the claimant does not intend to return.
-- home, other: the claimant meets the payment and liability conditions for the home accommodation, for the other accommodation; homeOk, otherOk: it is reasonable to include an amount for each.
GIVEN apply IS A NUMBER
      home IS A BOOLEAN
      other IS A BOOLEAN
      homeOk IS A BOOLEAN
      otherOk IS A BOOLEAN
      first IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Claimant living in other accommodation because of fear of violence`
`uc3 test — a claimant living elsewhere for fear of violence` apply home other homeOk otherOk first day MEANS
    `Claimant living in other accommodation because of fear of violence` WITH
        `the claimant is occupying accommodation other than the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home` IS NOT (apply EQUALS 1)
        `it is unreasonable to expect the claimant to return to the home accommodation on account of the claimant's reasonable fear of violence in the home, or by a former partner, against the claimant or any child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant is responsible` IS NOT (apply EQUALS 2)
        `the claimant intends to return to the home accommodation` IS NOT (apply EQUALS 3)
        `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the home accommodation` IS home
        `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the other accommodation` IS other
        `it is reasonable to include an amount in the housing costs element for the payments in respect of the home accommodation` IS homeOk
        `it is reasonable to include an amount in the housing costs element for the payments in respect of the other accommodation` IS otherOk
        `first day on which the claimant is treated as occupying both accommodations` IS first
        `day to which the question relates` IS day

-- Paragraph 6(1): all three of (a), (b), (c). Expected: all three gives TRUE; each missing gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 6(1) — this paragraph applies` (`uc3 test — a claimant living elsewhere for fear of violence` 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 6(1) — this paragraph applies` (`uc3 test — a claimant living elsewhere for fear of violence` 1 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 6(1) — this paragraph applies` (`uc3 test — a claimant living elsewhere for fear of violence` 2 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 6(1) — this paragraph applies` (`uc3 test — a claimant living elsewhere for fear of violence` 3 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
-- Paragraph 6(2): both accommodations if the payment and liability conditions are met for both and it is reasonable to include an amount for both (here also within 12 months, from 6(4)).
-- Expected: both met, both reasonable, on 31 December 2025 (12 months from 1 January 2025 not exceeded) gives TRUE; on 1 January 2026 gives FALSE; only one reasonable gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 6(2) — the claimant is treated as normally occupying both` (`uc3 test — a claimant living elsewhere for fear of violence` 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 12 31)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 6(2) — the claimant is treated as normally occupying both` (`uc3 test — a claimant living elsewhere for fear of violence` 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 6(2) — the claimant is treated as normally occupying both` (`uc3 test — a claimant living elsewhere for fear of violence` 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 3 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 6(2) — the claimant is treated as normally occupying both` (`uc3 test — a claimant living elsewhere for fear of violence` 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 3 1)) EQUALS FALSE
-- The whole of paragraph 6. Expected: both conditions and both reasonable, within 12 months, gives both accommodations; the home only (conditions met for the home only, and reasonable) gives the home only;
-- the other only gives the other only; one only but not reasonable gives neither; paragraph 6 not applying gives neither;
-- both after 12 months gives the explicit not-covered value (fork U3-F20: the text says only that the claimant may not be treated as occupying both for more than 12 months).
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 6 — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying` (`uc3 test — a claimant living elsewhere for fear of violence` 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 12 31)) EQUALS `both the home accommodation and the other accommodation`
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 6 — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying` (`uc3 test — a claimant living elsewhere for fear of violence` 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 3 1)) EQUALS `the home accommodation only`
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 6 — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying` (`uc3 test — a claimant living elsewhere for fear of violence` 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 3 1)) EQUALS `the other accommodation only`
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 6 — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying` (`uc3 test — a claimant living elsewhere for fear of violence` 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 3 1)) EQUALS `neither: paragraph 6 does not treat the claimant as occupying either`
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 6 — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying` (`uc3 test — a claimant living elsewhere for fear of violence` 3 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 3 1)) EQUALS `neither: paragraph 6 does not treat the claimant as occupying either`
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 6 — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying` (`uc3 test — a claimant living elsewhere for fear of violence` 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1)) EQUALS `not covered: the text does not say which accommodation the claimant is treated as occupying once the 12 months of paragraph 6(4) have passed`
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 6(3) — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying where one only meets the conditions` (`uc3 test — a claimant living elsewhere for fear of violence` 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 3 1)) EQUALS `the home accommodation only`

-- Paragraph 7: moving in delayed by adaptations. miss: 0 nothing missing; 1 not since moved in; 2 conditions not met immediately before the move; 3 no necessary delay; 4 the person is not specified; 5 the delay was not reasonable.
GIVEN miss IS A NUMBER
      first IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Move that was delayed by adaptations to accommodation`
`uc3 test — a delayed move` miss first day MEANS
    `Move that was delayed by adaptations to accommodation` WITH
        `the claimant has since moved in` IS NOT (miss EQUALS 1)
        `immediately before the move the claimant met the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the accommodation` IS NOT (miss EQUALS 2)
        `there was a delay in moving in that was necessary to enable the accommodation to be adapted to meet the disablement needs of a relevant person` IS NOT (miss EQUALS 3)
        `the relevant person` IS `uc3 test — a person who may be specified` TRUE (NOT (miss EQUALS 4))
        `it was reasonable to delay moving in` IS NOT (miss EQUALS 5)
        `first day on which the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation` IS first
        `day to which the question relates` IS day
-- Expected: nothing missing within one month (31 January 2025 from 1 January 2025) gives TRUE; on 1 February 2025 gives FALSE (7(3)); each of the five missing gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 7 — the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation before moving in` (`uc3 test — a delayed move` 0 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 31)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 7 — the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation before moving in` (`uc3 test — a delayed move` 0 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 2 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 7 — the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation before moving in` (`uc3 test — a delayed move` 1 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 7 — the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation before moving in` (`uc3 test — a delayed move` 2 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 7 — the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation before moving in` (`uc3 test — a delayed move` 3 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 7 — the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation before moving in` (`uc3 test — a delayed move` 4 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 7 — the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation before moving in` (`uc3 test — a delayed move` 5 (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS FALSE

-- Paragraph 8: moving in following a stay in hospital or a care home. A person's situation when the liability arose: a patient (in-patient treatment), or accommodated in a care home.
GIVEN patient IS A BOOLEAN
      accommodated IS A BOOLEAN
      isCareHome IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person's situation when a liability arose`
`uc3 test — a person's situation` patient accommodated isCareHome MEANS
    `Person's situation when a liability arose` WITH
        `the person was undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient in any hospital or similar institution` IS patient
        `the care home in which the person was accommodated` IS `uc3 test — premises that may be a care home` isCareHome
        `the person was accommodated in that care home` IS accommodated
-- Expected: a patient gives TRUE; a person accommodated in a care home gives TRUE; accommodated in premises that are not a care home gives FALSE; neither gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 8(1)(b) — the person was a patient or accommodated in a care home` (`uc3 test — a person's situation` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 8(1)(b) — the person was a patient or accommodated in a care home` (`uc3 test — a person's situation` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 8(1)(b) — the person was a patient or accommodated in a care home` (`uc3 test — a person's situation` FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 8(1)(b) — the person was a patient or accommodated in a care home` (`uc3 test — a person's situation` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

GIVEN basis IS A `Claim basis`
      first IS A `Person's situation when a liability arose`
      second IS A `Person's situation when a liability arose`
      day IS A DATE
      moved IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Move following a stay in hospital or a care home`
`uc3 test — a move after a stay` basis first second day moved MEANS
    `Move following a stay in hospital or a care home` WITH
        `the claimant has since moved in` IS moved
        `immediately before the move the claimant met the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the accommodation` IS TRUE
        `claim basis` IS basis
        `the situation of the claimant when the liability to make the payments arose` IS first
        `the situation of the other joint claimant when the liability to make the payments arose` IS second
        `first day on which the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation` IS YMD 2025 1 1
        `day to which the question relates` IS day
-- Expected: a single claimant who was a patient, within one month (31 January 2025), gives TRUE; on 1 February 2025 gives FALSE (8(2));
-- joint claimants of whom only one was a patient give FALSE ("while both joint claimants were patients"); both give TRUE; not yet moved in gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 8 — the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation before moving in` (`uc3 test — a move after a stay` `a single claimant` (`uc3 test — a person's situation` TRUE FALSE FALSE) (`uc3 test — a person's situation` FALSE FALSE FALSE) (YMD 2025 1 31) TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 8 — the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation before moving in` (`uc3 test — a move after a stay` `a single claimant` (`uc3 test — a person's situation` TRUE FALSE FALSE) (`uc3 test — a person's situation` FALSE FALSE FALSE) (YMD 2025 2 1) TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 8 — the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation before moving in` (`uc3 test — a move after a stay` `joint claimants` (`uc3 test — a person's situation` TRUE FALSE FALSE) (`uc3 test — a person's situation` FALSE FALSE FALSE) (YMD 2025 1 31) TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 8 — the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation before moving in` (`uc3 test — a move after a stay` `joint claimants` (`uc3 test — a person's situation` TRUE FALSE FALSE) (`uc3 test — a person's situation` FALSE TRUE TRUE) (YMD 2025 1 31) TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 8 — the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation before moving in` (`uc3 test — a move after a stay` `a single claimant` (`uc3 test — a person's situation` TRUE FALSE FALSE) (`uc3 test — a person's situation` FALSE FALSE FALSE) (YMD 2025 1 31) FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 2, paragraph 9: a temporary absence that exceeds, or is expected to exceed, 6 months ends the occupation, except for a claimant within paragraph 3 (never), and 12 months for a claimant within paragraph 6.
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      expectedEnd IS A DATE
      withinThree IS A BOOLEAN
      withinSix IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Temporary absence from accommodation`
`uc3 test — a temporary absence` day expectedEnd withinThree withinSix MEANS
    `Temporary absence from accommodation` WITH
        `first day of the absence` IS YMD 2025 1 1
        `day to which the question relates` IS day
        `last day to which the absence is expected to last` IS expectedEnd
        `the claimant falls within paragraph 3` IS withinThree
        `the claimant falls within paragraph 6` IS withinSix
-- Expected for the test of a number of months: from 1 January 2025, 30 June 2025 does not exceed 6 months (FALSE) and 1 July 2025 does (TRUE); an absence on 30 June 2025 that is expected to last to 1 July 2025 is expected to exceed 6 months (TRUE).
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 9 — the absence exceeds, or is expected to exceed, a number of months` (`uc3 test — a temporary absence` (YMD 2025 6 30) (YMD 2025 6 30) FALSE FALSE) 6 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 9 — the absence exceeds, or is expected to exceed, a number of months` (`uc3 test — a temporary absence` (YMD 2025 7 1) (YMD 2025 7 1) FALSE FALSE) 6 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 9 — the absence exceeds, or is expected to exceed, a number of months` (`uc3 test — a temporary absence` (YMD 2025 6 30) (YMD 2025 7 1) FALSE FALSE) 6 EQUALS TRUE
-- Paragraph 9 as a whole. Expected: an ordinary claimant is treated as no longer occupying once 6 months are exceeded (TRUE on 1 July, FALSE on 30 June) or expected to be (TRUE);
-- a claimant within paragraph 3 never (FALSE even on 1 July 2026); a claimant within paragraph 6 only after 12 months: FALSE on 1 July 2025, FALSE on 31 December 2025, TRUE on 1 January 2026,
-- and TRUE on 30 June 2025 if the absence is expected to last to 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 9 — the claimant is treated as no longer occupying the accommodation` (`uc3 test — a temporary absence` (YMD 2025 6 30) (YMD 2025 6 30) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 9 — the claimant is treated as no longer occupying the accommodation` (`uc3 test — a temporary absence` (YMD 2025 7 1) (YMD 2025 7 1) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 9 — the claimant is treated as no longer occupying the accommodation` (`uc3 test — a temporary absence` (YMD 2025 6 30) (YMD 2025 12 31) FALSE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 9 — the claimant is treated as no longer occupying the accommodation` (`uc3 test — a temporary absence` (YMD 2026 7 1) (YMD 2026 7 1) TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 9 — the claimant is treated as no longer occupying the accommodation` (`uc3 test — a temporary absence` (YMD 2025 7 1) (YMD 2025 7 1) FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 9 — the claimant is treated as no longer occupying the accommodation` (`uc3 test — a temporary absence` (YMD 2025 12 31) (YMD 2025 12 31) FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 9 — the claimant is treated as no longer occupying the accommodation` (`uc3 test — a temporary absence` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 3 para 9 — the claimant is treated as no longer occupying the accommodation` (`uc3 test — a temporary absence` (YMD 2025 6 30) (YMD 2026 1 1) FALSE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
